---
import PageLayout from "../../layouts/PageLayout.astro"
import Picture from "../../components/Picture.astro"
import { formatDate } from "../../utils/date"
import { livecodingCollection } from "../../data/livecoding-collection"
import { getGigs } from "../../utils/gigs"

const gigs = (await getGigs()).map((gig) => ({
  title: gig.data.title,
  url: gig.url,
  dateStr: gig.data.date,
  dateFormatted: formatDate(new Date(gig.data.date)),
  venue: gig.data.venue,
  slug: gig.id,
}))

const firstYear = gigs.at(-1)?.dateStr.slice(0, 4)
const lastYear = gigs.at(0)?.dateStr.slice(0, 4)
---

<PageLayout title="Livecoding" relativePath="src/pages/livecoding/index.astro">
  <Picture
    file="livecoding/smcclab-live-1.webp"
    alt="Livecoding performance at SMCClab live #1 in Nov 2025"
  />

  <p>
    The nature of livecoding is that it is performed (improvised) in-the-moment; the
    gig (performance) <em>is</em> the output (that's why it's called <strong>live</strong>coding), and
    any artefact (e.g. a video recording) is useful documentation, but only a trace
    of the work itself.
  </p>

  <p>
    Still, documentation is an important part of one's artistic practice, so here's
    a bunch of photos and videos from my gigs. Some of them are nice &amp;
    slick-looking, some of them are super-grungy videos shot on smartphones in the
    crowd. Although I'm working hard to track down any old videos, some of these
    gigs are lost to time. I like to assume that they were the best ones ;)
  </p>

  <p>
    Taken together, these {gigs.length} performances span {firstYear}&ndash;{lastYear}:
    nearly two decades of live-coding practice, gathered here as a single body of work.
    Each one is increasingly being given its own DataCite DOI so it can be cited as a
    research output in its own right.
  </p>

  <p>
    There's also a more formal <a href="/livecoding/research-statement/">research statement</a> for
    the body of work, with notes on a handful of the anchor gigs, if that's your sort of thing.
  </p>

  {livecodingCollection && (
    <p class="collection-cite">
      Cite the body of work:{" "}
      <a href={livecodingCollection.doiUrl}>{livecodingCollection.conceptDoi}</a>
      {" · "}
      <a href={livecodingCollection.community.url}>Zenodo community</a>
    </p>
  )}

  <hr />

  <ul class="post-list">
    {gigs.map((gig) => (
      <li class="post-item">
        <a href={gig.url} class="post-item-title">{gig.title}</a>
        <span class="post-item-date">{gig.dateFormatted}</span>
        {gig.venue && <span class="post-item-venue"> - {gig.venue}</span>}
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
</PageLayout>
